            },
            "displayName": "Doron Cohen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Gaza"
          },
          "body": "> You mean for some of the fields, using Fieldable's setOmitNorms(). \n\nOops, just noticed this was already suggested that in that for that user thread...\n\nAnyhow, for that specific scenario seems omitNorms would be sufficient, but it won't help the db based example above.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=doronc",
            "name": "doronc",
            "key": "doronc",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
